  "summary": "Two meshing spur gears turn inside a close-fitting figure-8 housing. On the inlet side the teeth come out of mesh, opening volume that draws liquid in; the liquid is carried around the outside of each gear in the tooth spaces and is displaced into the outlet where the teeth re-mesh. Flow is nearly proportional to speed; pressure is set by the system, so over-pressure protection (relief valve) is essential.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Positive displacement – rotary",
    "configuration": "External gear, two shafts, gears supported between bearings (sleeve bushings)",
    "drive": "One driven (drive) gear transmits torque to the idler through the tooth mesh"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "gears": "12 teeth, module 6 mm, pressure angle 25°, face width 60 mm",
    "centre_distance_mm": 72.00000000000001,
    "theoretical_displacement_note": "Approximate geometric displacement per revolution ≈ 2·π·m²·z·b (standard-gear approximation); with these values ≈ 0.16 L/rev. Verify any real pump against manufacturer data.",
    "theoretical_displacement_l_per_rev": 0.163,
    "shaft_seal": "Single mechanical seal in rear cover",
    "relief_valve": "Integral spring-loaded poppet valve, discharge → suction (internal recirculation)",
    "rotation": "Drive gear clockwise viewed from the drive-shaft end (rear); inlet on left, outlet on right in default view"
  },
